  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (PCA n2000, single profile) achieves 0.485 accuracy, clearly outperforming image (ResNet50) at 0.208, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether leveraging multiple profiles with simple aggregation (avgpool) can improve upon the single-profile RNA baseline. This experiment (config_002) tests multiprofile + avgpool while keeping the same PCA n2000 encoder, isolating the effect of profile multiplicity and aggregation. It is the best next step because it is a minimal, single-variable extension of the current best result, will tell us whether multiprofile is a productive direction before investing in more complex aggregations (transformer) or alternative encoders (scvi, scgpt), and preserves budget for follow-up experiments if multiprofile proves beneficial."
}

